// The k0-seek-path member of the 0919 family: a DRIVER predicate joined on
// the anchor-shared var routes the since read through the correlated k0
// path (`to_join_on_since_key`) instead of the standalone read, so the
// same-step guard check there is keyed by the DRIVER's value (`_drv`), not
// the anchor row's.
//
// With a single event per step the driver pins `x` to the current event's
// server, so the foreign-mismatch trap of 0919 cannot fire here — this case
// is the OVER-CONSTRAINT control for the k0 path: a MATCHING same-step
// heartbeat (@10, streak seeded in the same statement) must still PERMIT
// after the guard check is keyed. @20 pins the no-anchor deny for a foreign
// server.
//
// Interpreter is the oracle (see expected_1.out).
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (x: String). (
        Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: x }
        && (Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: x }
            since within 1h
            Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.server: x })
    )
};
